%% DocuTrust share link lifecycle (Mermaid source) - includes the Phase 5 OTP gate
stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> Created : owner mints share\npermission view|download\nexpiresAt, maxViews?, passcode?\nrequireOtp? + recipientEmail (V11)
    Created --> Active : link_token issued (43 chars)\npasscode PBKDF2-hashed
    Created --> OTP_Locked : require_otp = true\n(V11 migration)

    OTP_Locked --> OTP_Locked : plain open -> 401 SHARE_OTP_REQUIRED\nrequest-otp emails the pinned inbox only\nwrong recipient -> 403 (no leak)
    OTP_Locked --> Active : open-with-otp succeeds\nemailed code verified (single use)\n+ passcode check -> atomic open

    Active --> Active : public open\natomic UPDATE view_count = view_count + 1\nWHERE not revoked AND not expired AND under max_views
    Active --> Expired : expires_at passed\nHTTP 410 GONE
    Active --> Revoked : owner revokes (instant)\nHTTP 409 SHARE_REVOKED
    Active --> Exhausted : view_count = max_views\nHTTP 409 SHARE_MAX_VIEWS
    Active --> Blocked : document deleted (410 GONE)\nor pending_review (403)

    Expired --> [*]
    Revoked --> [*]
    Exhausted --> [*]
    Blocked --> [*]

    note right of OTP_Locked
        OTP gate (Phase 5):
        each open costs one emailed code -
        the code is single-use and burned at 5
        wrong attempts; the API never reveals
        the designated recipient address
    end note

    note right of Active
        download permission requires a
        single-use 5-minute ticket
        (/api/public/download/:ticket)
        archived documents (rejected review):
        existing links stay usable -
        only hard delete kills a link
    end note
